---
title: Miso Glazed Roasted Cabbage
servings: 2
prep-time: 15 minutes
cook-time: 25 minutes
tags: [vegetarian, thanksgiving, recipe, cabbage, roasted]
source: https://www.instagram.com/reel/DRAfKcoEnRH/
image: https://scontent-iad3-2.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.71878-15/582838730_2061981114620565_4189558456759927873_n.jpg?stp=cmp1_dst-jpg_e35_s640x640_tt6&_nc_cat=111&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=18de74&efg=eyJlZmdfdGFnIjoiQ0xJUFMuYmVzdF9pbWFnZV91cmxnZW4uQzIifQ%3D%3D&_nc_ohc=OBWdsvK95R0Q7kNvwF2kMEo&_nc_oc=Adml67FHGL9LYXMf1UD9tnJSLykEtE4Fv-ekR_YRT8x4akuKDXIKeCBnnB5tp3ISfc8&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-2.cdninstagram.com&_nc_gid=KQgnI3Gp2nOuCY5egoOlLg&oh=00_AfmJ6F4tJfMLnsAe2GZ_o8NJlfXb58OSvusx71_Z90wGkA&oe=694E502E
---

Preheat your #oven to 400°F. Arrange @cabbage{1%head} wedges on a #baking sheet{} lined with parchment paper.

In a small bowl whisk together @miso paste{2%tbsp}, @honey{2%tbsp}, @lemon juice{1%tbsp}, and @tahini{2%tbsp} to form the glaze. Brush the cabbage with half of this glaze.

Roast the cabbage in the oven for ~{25%minutes}, turning once halfway through and brushing with the remaining glaze, until the edges are caramelized and the cabbage is tender.

To serve, plate the roasted cabbage over a bed of @tahini{0.5%cup} sauce and garnish with @chives{1%tbsp}.